sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  box rgb(237,243,248) Control plane
    participant O as OCC<br/>local IAM
    participant S as State store
  end
  box rgb(235,243,240) Worker process
    participant W as Worker<br/>Compute Driver
  end
  participant K as Kubernetes<br/>runtime
  participant G as Trusted<br/>gateway
  participant C as Dedicated Codex<br/>gVisor
  participant M as Model provider
  participant R as Repository<br/>service

  Note over U,R: 1 · Authorize and admit an immutable revision
  U->>O: Request deployment with approved repository selection
  O->>O: Authorize Agent and validate profile
  O->>S: Persist revision and explicit storage policy in original transaction
  S-->>O: Admitted revision
  O-->>U: Accepted deployment

  Note over U,R: 2 · Prepare exact owned resources and observe candidates
  W->>S: Claim admitted work
  S-->>W: Immutable revision and owned work
  W->>W: Reauthorize immutable revision through local IAM
  Note over W,K: Retained successor path first requires writer exclusion.<br/>See storage and recovery before any writable preparation.
  W->>K: Prepare original owned resources and role workloads
  K-->>W: Original identities and complete candidate observation
  W->>W: Check class and one eligible Ready Pod
  alt Positive isolation violation
    W->>K: Conditionally withdraw affected route and request UID-guarded cleanup
    K-->>W: Observed result or explicit uncertainty
    Note over W,K: Preserve successor resources and late cleanup custody.<br/>Unavailable evidence alone authorizes no deletion.
  else Safe observation permits continued preparation
    W->>R: Open or recover admitted session within original deadline
    R-->>W: Ephemeral session material or unavailable outcome
    W->>K: Deliver only to Codex and observe exact material generation
    K-->>W: No old-generation candidates and one expected Ready Pod
    W->>W: Reauthorize before activation
    W->>S: Commit selected revision
    S-->>W: Selected revision committed
    W->>K: Activate exact revision route and verify readiness
    K-->>W: Activation observed or unavailable
    Note over W,K: Default post-commit activation shown.
    Note over W,K: beforeCommit Drivers verify activation before selection.
  end

  Note over U,R: 3 · Complete an ordinary authorized contribution
  opt Exact revision activated and request authorized
  U->>G: Submit authenticated repository task
  G->>C: Invoke dedicated Harness for admitted request
  C->>M: Dispatch admitted model request
  M-->>C: Model result
  C->>R: Managed Git clone through admitted session
  R-->>C: Repository contents
  C->>C: Real tool children edit, test and commit
  C->>R: Managed Git push and approved same-repository PR
  R-->>C: Provider outcome, subject to independent readback
  C-->>G: Task result and contribution evidence
  G-->>U: Authorized result
  end
  Note over G,R: Protected profile adds requester, identity and closure gates.<br/>Never blindly replay uncertain remote effects.

  Note over U,R: 4 · Close access, then observe exact runtime stop
  W->>R: Close session and retain unresolved provider cleanup
  R-->>W: Local closure and known cleanup disposition
  W->>K: Withdraw exact revision route and stop its workloads
  K-->>W: Termination evidence or unavailable / unverified outcome
  W->>S: Retain observed result and pending cleanup custody
  Note over W,K: Accepted deletion is not observed physical stop.<br/>Disposal follows admitted policy. Retained stop preserves data.
  Note over U,R: Entire lifecycle is proposed. Time flows downward.<br/>Solid arrows are requests. Dashed arrows are replies.
